      "Best UCs for Biology / Life Sciences: UCSD is the clear leader — adjacent to Scripps Research, the Salk Institute, and UCSD Health; many undergraduates do lab work at these institutions. UCLA Life Sciences is comparably strong, especially molecular, cell, and developmental biology, supported by the David Geffen School of Medicine. Berkeley Molecular and Cell Biology (MCB) and Integrative Biology (IB) are top 5 nationally. UC Davis is exceptional for biological sciences with an agricultural and environmental slant, and is home to the top veterinary school in the world. UC Irvine has strong biological sciences and biomedical research tied to UCI Health. UCSB Marine Biology is excellent given coastal location.",
      "Best UCs for Business: Berkeley Haas is the only UC with direct freshman admission to a traditional undergraduate business major — the Haas BS in Business Administration admits freshmen via a separate supplementary application and is top 3 nationally. UC Riverside's School of Business offers direct freshman admission to its business major and is AACSB-accredited. Every other UC (UCLA, UCSD, UCI, UC Davis, UCSB, UCSC, UC Merced) offers Business Economics or Economics at the undergraduate level and routes serious business-track students through those majors plus a business minor — there is no direct freshman undergraduate business major at those campuses. UCLA Anderson and UC Irvine Merage are well-known but are graduate-only business schools for undergrads.",
      "Best UCs for Physics / Math: Berkeley Mathematics and Berkeley Physics are top 5 nationally. UCSB Physics is elite — the Kavli Institute for Theoretical Physics and the Materials Research Lab are on campus, and UCSB physicists have received five Nobel Prizes since 1998. UCLA Physics and Math are top 15. UCSD Physics has strong condensed matter and particle physics; Math is top 20. UC Davis and UC Irvine have solid but mid-tier programs. UC Santa Cruz has outstanding physics research output relative to its size, particularly in astrophysics.",
      "Best UCs for Astronomy / Astrophysics: UC Santa Cruz is the UC leader for astronomy — it hosts the UC Observatories headquarters, operates Lick Observatory, leads the Thirty Meter Telescope collaboration, and consistently ranks in the global top 10 for astronomy research output. Berkeley Astronomy is top 5 nationally. UCLA Physics and Astronomy is top 10. UCSD has a rapidly growing astrophysics group. UC Riverside has a notable astrobiology program.",
      "Best UCs for Film, Media, and the Arts: UCLA's School of Theater, Film, and Television is top 3 nationally alongside USC and NYU — direct industry pipeline to Hollywood. UCSB Film and Media Studies is highly respected and Oscar-dense in alumni. UC Santa Cruz has a strong Film and Digital Media program. UC Irvine has the Claire Trevor School of the Arts with a notable drama program (UCI's MFA in Acting is top-tier). Berkeley does not have a dedicated film school but has strong Film and Media Studies within the College of Letters & Science.",
      "Best UCs for Cognitive Science / Psychology: UC San Diego invented the modern academic discipline of Cognitive Science (the first Cog Sci department in the world opened at UCSD in 1986) and is consistently ranked #1 — offers specializations in Machine Learning and Neural Computation, Language and Culture, Neuroscience, and HCI. UCLA Psychology is top 5. Berkeley Psychology is top 10. UC Irvine Cognitive Science and Psychology are both strong. UC Davis Psychology has a distinctive animal cognition track.",
      "Best UCs for Environmental Studies / Sustainability / Marine Biology: UCSB Bren School of Environmental Science and Management is top 5 nationally for environmental programs. UC Santa Cruz Environmental Studies is historically one of the first undergraduate programs in the country and remains top-tier. UC Davis is the national leader in agricultural and environmental policy — top in sustainability, plant sciences, and viticulture. UCSD has Scripps Institution of Oceanography for marine-focused students. UC Merced's Sierra Nevada Research Institute grounds its sustainability emphasis.",
