      "UC Merced is a public research university in Merced, California — the newest campus in the University of California system, which opened in 2005 as the first American research university built in the 21st century. Undergraduate enrollment is approximately 9,000. The Fall 2024 admit rate was approximately 86%, making UC Merced the most accessible UC and a particularly strong option for students who are UC-eligible but not competitive for Berkeley, UCLA, UCSD, or UCSB.",
